{
  // Review follow-up N6 (2026-08-09) — nothing in CI typechecked `scripts/`.
  //
  // `tsconfig.lint.json` is `include: ["src/**/*"], exclude: ["test/**/*"]`
  // and `tsconfig.build.json` is src-only, so every operational script was
  // covered by NO gate, and no CI job runs one. That is exactly how
  // `scripts/seed-voice-quality-cassettes.ts` came to fail its `ts-node`
  // typecheck: `test/voice-quality/voice-quality-driver-factory.ts`'s
  // hand-rolled `SettingsRepository` stub went stale when the interface grew
  // a method, and vitest's esbuild transform does not typecheck, so nothing
  // caught it until someone ran the script by hand.
  //
  // Scope, deliberately narrow: the `scripts/` tree plus the ONE test-tree
  // helper a script imports. The rest of `test/**` is not included — it is
  // large, already exercised by vitest, and pulling it in here would turn a
  // fast, targeted gate into a second full typecheck.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "..",
    "types": ["vitest/globals", "node"]
  },
  "include": [
    "scripts/**/*.ts",
    "test/voice-quality/voice-quality-driver-factory.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    // The ONE pre-existing failure this gate surfaced, scoped out rather
    // than allowed to sink the whole check:
    //   scripts/voice-load-selfcheck.ts(38,34): error TS1343: The
    //   'import.meta' meta-property is only allowed when the '--module'
    //   option is 'es2020' | ... | 'nodenext'.
    // It is an ESM-shaped script run under `tsx` (`npm run
    // voice-load:selfcheck`), so it is genuinely incompatible with this
    // package's commonjs `module` setting — not a type error in its logic.
    // Typechecking it needs its own ESM tsconfig; that is a separate change,
    // and blocking this gate on it would mean shipping no gate at all.
    "scripts/voice-load-selfcheck.ts"
  ]
}
